[t9] Safety Auditor: That's a good plan, but I want to make sure we're not setting up a temporary redirect that's going to cause more problems down the line - we need to make sure it's a clean redirect, not a redirect that's going to cause a loop or other issues.

[t10] Operations Lead: We'll use a 301 permanent redirect, which will update the DNS records and ensure that the new endpoint is cached by browsers and other clients, minimizing the chance of a loop or other issues. I'll also make sure to test the redirect thoroughly before we fail over the API.

